  "pc1_selection_verdict": "PC1_UNFIT_FOR_SELECTING_A_STRUCTURED_PANEL. The plan pre-registered 'the intact panel with the highest measured pc1_variance_fraction' as the positive control. Measured, that rule is self-contradictory on this panel set: by raw pc1 the ordering is bxd > bloom > dgrp > arabmagic, and by excess-over-its-own-null it is bloom > bxd > arabmagic > dgrp -- so under BOTH normalisations the one NATURAL population (dgrp) ranks last or third, and under excess the top panel is BLOOM, the bi-parental cross that must be the NEGATIVE control. Mechanism, which is structural rather than statistical: pc1 measures total genotypic correlation = LD + structure, and a bi-parental cross maximises LD by construction while carrying no population structure. The control pair is therefore selected BY CONSTRUCTION from each panel's `design` field (declared before any number was read), with cluster SHAPE as independent corroboration -- not by pc1.",
  "fold_compatible_panels": [
    "bloom",
    "arabmagic",
    "bxd"
  ],
  "honest_limits": [
    "A census bounds INTEGRITY and STRUCTURE only. It says nothing about whether a panel's phenotypes are usable, nor whether its grouping is the right one.",
    "`design` is recorded by CONSTRUCTION (how the panel was built), not measured. pc1_variance_fraction is the measured statistic.",
    "A clean cluster shape is NOT evidence of structure: a percentile threshold manufactures well-shaped clusters on an unstructured panel (measured in eval/panel_structure.py). Read pc1_variance_fraction for existence.",
    "pc1 cannot SELECT a structured panel -- see pc1_selection_verdict. It conflates linkage disequilibrium with population structure, and a bi-parental cross maximises the former while having none of the latter.",
    "pc1_excess uses 3 permutations at 1200 subsampled markers: enough to establish an ordering, not a precise effect size."
  ]
